WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.079
Step 1. Open the Files tab.

1.2
00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:06.143
The patient and each encounter have separate lists of files.

1.3
00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.384
Open the patient page or the encounter page, and select the Files tab.

2.1
00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:16.834
Step 2. Select the Files sub-tab. Care opens the Files sub-tab first.

2.2
00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:22.157
The Reports sub-tab lists generated reports, not uploaded files.

3.1
00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:26.974
Step 3. Search by name. Type a part of the file name in Search files.

3.2
00:00:26.974 --> 00:00:30.349
Care lists the files whose name contains that text,

3.3
00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:33.033
whatever the case of the letters.

4.1
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:38.045
Step 4. Filter by status. By default, Status has All selected,

4.2
00:00:38.045 --> 00:00:42.115
so the list shows active and archived files together.

4.3
00:00:42.115 --> 00:00:46.531
Select Active or Archived to show only those files.

5.1
00:00:46.531 --> 00:00:48.601
Step 5. Read the list.

5.2
00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:55.134
Care shows the newest files first, with 15 files on each page, under File Name,

5.3
00:00:55.134 --> 00:00:58.115
File Type, Shared By and Date.

6.1
00:00:58.115 --> 00:01:03.959
Step 7. See why a file was archived. An archived file has the Archived badge.

6.2
00:01:03.959 --> 00:01:09.917
Point to the badge, or select View in its row, to see the reason, who archived it,

6.3
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:11.071
and when.
